# Governance Framework
## Digital Mental Health NLP Pipeline for Asian Adolescents

**Last Updated:** May 2026

---

## Overview

This document defines the governance framework for responsible deployment of the Digital Mental Health NLP Pipeline in Singapore school and community settings.

> This pipeline is currently a research project. Real-world deployment requires full compliance with this framework before any pilot begins.

---

## 1. Guiding Principles

| Principle | Description |
|---|---|
| **Do No Harm** | Clinical safety takes absolute priority |
| **Privacy by Design** | Data minimisation built into architecture |
| **Transparency** | Every risk score is explainable |
| **Equity** | Must not disadvantage any demographic group |
| **Accountability** | Clear human responsibility for every output |
| **Proportionality** | Minimum data collected and retained |

---

## 2. Legal and Regulatory Framework

| Regulation | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **PDPA** | Consent, purpose limitation, data minimisation |
| **Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act** | Mandatory reporting for imminent risk |
| **Children and Young Persons Act** | Parental consent required under 18 |
| **MOH Mental Health Framework** | Alignment with national care pathways |
| **MOE Data Governance Framework** | School board approval required |

**Before any pilot:**
- [ ] IRB/Ethics Committee approval
- [ ] MOH endorsement
- [ ] MOE school principal approval
- [ ] REACH team partnership agreement
- [ ] IMH emergency escalation protocol signed

