## 3. Data Governance

### 3.1 Data Classification

| Data Type | Sensitivity | Retention |
|---|---|---|
| Raw social media text | **Highest** | 0 days — never stored |
| Anonymised feature vectors | High | 30 days rolling |
| Risk scores | High | 90 days |
| Aggregated population data | Medium | 12 months |
| Audit logs | Low | 24 months |

### 3.2 Data Flow
Raw Text Input
│
▼ (feature extraction)
RAW TEXT DELETED ──────────────► Feature Vectors Only
│
▼
Model Inference
│
▼
Risk Score → Clinical Review Interface
│
▼
Action logged in audit trail
### 3.3 Data Minimisation

- No names or identifiers stored with feature vectors
- No raw text retained after feature extraction
- Purpose limitation — screening only; cannot be used for academic assessment or discipline
- Data processed and stored within Singapore only

---

## 4. Consent Framework

### 4.1 Consent by Age

| Age Group | Consent Required From |
|---|---|
| Under 16 | Parent/guardian + adolescent assent |
| 16–17 | Parent/guardian + adolescent |
| 18+ | Individual only |

### 4.2 Consent Must Cover

1. What data is collected
2. How it is processed (NLP, not human reading)
3. What outputs are generated (risk scores, not diagnoses)
4. Who sees the outputs (counsellors only)
5. What actions may follow (counsellor outreach, not automatic referral)
6. Right to withdraw at any time without consequence
7. Data retention and deletion schedule
8. Limitations of the system

### 4.3 Opt-In Only

Participation is strictly opt-in. No passive collection without explicit consent. No consequences for declining.

---

## 5. Access Control

| Role | Access Level |
|---|---|
| **Student** | Own risk trend only (optional) |
| **School Counsellor** | Risk scores for their school only |
| **REACH Officer** | Full output for escalated cases |
| **Institution Admin** | Aggregate anonymised statistics only |
| **Researcher** | Fully de-identified data + ethics approval |
| **System Admin** | Audit logs only — no clinical data |

All clinical data access is logged with user ID, timestamp, records accessed, and action taken.

---

## 6. Clinical Accountability

### 6.1 Responsibility Chain

Pipeline Output (automated)
│
▼
School Counsellor Review (mandatory — human)
│
├── Low/Medium Risk → Counsellor decides action
│
└── High Risk → REACH Officer within 2 hours
│
├── Crisis imminent → IMH / Emergency services
└── Not imminent → Care plan developed
### 6.2 Incident Review

For every missed case or adverse event — review within 14 days covering:
- What the pipeline flagged (or missed)
- What clinical action was taken
- Contributing factors
- Changes required

---

## 7. Model Governance

### 7.1 Validation Requirements

| Validation | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Technical | AUC > 0.85, Sensitivity > 80% |
| Clinical | Validated against Singapore counsellor assessments |
| Equity | No significant performance gap across ethnicity/gender/SES |

### 7.2 Ongoing Monitoring

| Metric | Frequency | Review Threshold |
|---|---|---|
| Model AUC | Monthly | Drop > 0.05 |
| False negative rate | Monthly | Rate > 15% |
| False positive rate | Monthly | Rate > 30% |
| Demographic parity | Quarterly | >10% gap across groups |

---

## 8. Research Use of Pipeline Data

Anonymised data may be used for research only if:
- [ ] Separate ethics approval obtained
- [ ] Data fully de-identified (k-anonymity ≥ 5)
- [ ] Findings shared back with participating schools
- [ ] No commercial use without explicit consent
- [ ] Raw data never leaves Singapore

---

## 9. Governance Review Schedule

| Review | Frequency |
|---|---|
